LL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://euans-guide-cms-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/2025_Euans_Guide_Access_Survey_Results_9b731bd4d2.pdf', '2026-09-02', NULL, NULL, 1, 'co1', 'GB', 'Disability-led, verified from the retrieved report. p.10, About Euan''s Guide: ''the award-winning disabled access charity best known for EuansGuide.com, the disabled access review website with thousands of reviews written by disabled people for disabled people''; ''The charity was set up by Euan MacDonald MBE and his sister Kiki in 2013 as a solution to poor disabled access information. Euan was diagnosed with Motor Neuron Disease in 2003 and when he became a wheelchair then powerchair user he discovered everyday activities were stressful due to a lack of disabled access information.'' p.3: ''Euan''s Guide - the disabled access charity - has listened to and amplified the voices of disabled people, their families, and carers''; ''Over 4,400 people shared their experiences in the most recent Access Survey.'' NOT IN THE DOCUMENT: no charity registration number appears anywhere in the 29 pages, so none is asserted here. FUNDING, ON THE FACE OF THE REPORT: the survey is ''supported by the Motability Scheme'' (p.3), Motability Operations supplies two of the three pull-quotes and an About page (p.9-10), and the report publishes no methodology at all - no sampling method, no fieldwork dates, no per-question base, no weighting - so sponsor-channel recruitment can be neither confirmed nor excluded.', 'dpo_annual_survey', NULL, 'GREY', 'VERIFIED', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-02 21:29', 'session_2026-09-02-research-batch-05-circulation-icf', '2026-09-02 22:03', 'session_2026-09-02-research-batch-05-circulation-icf', 'retrieval_log', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'CORRECTED', '2026-09-02 co1_provenance CORRECTED (the previous text cited p.2 and p.28 for the provenance and asserted it was verified from the report rather than from a description of it. p.2 of this PDF is blank apart from the running header, p.28 is survey question 40, and the charity registration number it carried appears nowhere in the 29 pages - it came from the exec-34 web description, which is what the sentence denied). Replaced text was: "Euan''s Guide, a disabled-led access charity (Scottish charity SC045492) set up in 2013 by Euan MacDonald MBE, a powerchair user, with his sister Kiki MacDonald. The report is the charity''s own annual survey of disabled people, their families and carers; over 4,400 shared their experiences in this round. Provenance verified from the retrieved report itself (p.2, p.28), not from a description of it." || 2026-09-02 verification_disposition CORRECTED (insert_source wrote every VERIFIED row with no CLOSED disposition, which D-0157 invariant I1 forbids; the default is fixed for new rows and these nine predate the fix). Replaced text was: None', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', 'not-applicable', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'CLOSED', 'tool', NULL);
